<title>USA: Pemberton, N.J., seeks tax hikes, layoffs -- paper.</title>
<headline>Pemberton, N.J., seeks tax hikes, layoffs -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pemberton, N.J., Board of Education proposed tax increases and layoffs to eliminate a $3.5 million budget deficit, the Philadelphia Inquirer reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>If approved, the district's $57.5 million spending plan would raise the school tax rate by 4.75 cents, from $1.28 to $1.33 per $100 of a property's assessed value.</p>
<p>In addition, the proposals would eliminate 41 district employees' jobs, the paper said.</p>
<p>District officials attributed the spending gap to federal aid cutbacks and the rising costs of special education.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
